	// For commands where output is combined? Actually for add etc, git output (commit) goes to stdout (grey). Git commit output is on stdout? Or stderr? Git commit prints to stdout? Let's see: git commit prints "[master ...] ..." to stdout? Actually it prints to stdout? In our earlier tests, git output for add was captured and printed grey to stdout. That output includes "[master ...]\n 1 file...\n create...". That's git's stdout? Or combined? We'll capture combined (stdout+stderr) for those?
